1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
Your tires are trying to
tell you something.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:07,400
Here are three signs it's
time for new ones.

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:09,700
Sign one — the penny test.

4
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:12,800
Flip a penny upside-down
into the tread.

5
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:15,500
If you can see all
of Lincoln's

6
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,300
head, your tread is too worn.

7
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:21,000
Sign two — cracks on the sidewall.

8
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,900
Weather and age dry out rubber,

9
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:26,900
and a cracked sidewall can
fail without warning.

10
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:30,200
Sign three — your car pulls
to one side,

11
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:33,600
or you feel a vibration
at highway speed.

12
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:35,500
That's uneven wear talking.

13
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:38,000
Bald tires take almost
twice as long

14
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,600
to stop in the rain.

15
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:42,900
That's not a small risk.

16
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:46,000
If you're not sure, a
free visual check

17
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,600
takes two minutes.

18
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:51,700
Nick's Tire Auto — stop by,
we'll check for free.
